I was considering that for a bit, actually. If we go that route, I think it would make sense to break up 
```c++
GETSET_PROPERTY(Windows::Foundation::IReference<guid>, Guid, nullptr);
```
into
```c++
// return/accept guid instead of IReference<guid>
bool HasGuid();
guid Guid();
void Guid(guid);
```
I ended up deciding against it because it'd be a bit of extra work. We could probably create a new `HASGETSET_OPTIONAL_PROPERTY` macro. On top of that, you can't have an `IReference<hstring>` so that's _extra_ annoying.

